{:edb/db-before-t 1591 :edb/db-after-t 1592 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534904 50 #inst "2026-10-08T10:35:20.969Z" 13194139534904 true] [17592186133860 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318669 13194139534904 true] [17592186133861 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318638 13194139534904 true] [17592186133861 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318645 13194139534904 true] [17592186133861 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318662 13194139534904 true] [17592186133862 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318651 13194139534904 true] [17592186318638 1017 #edb/ref 17592186318639 13194139534904 true] [17592186318638 1089 "q-116612" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318638 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534904 true] [17592186318638 1100 "Solve the inequality $4{x}^{2}-{x}^{4}<0.$" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318638 1113 #uuid "f6df953a-e0ea-50a9-90ed-096dcc70da47" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318638 1145 "First, we factor the polynomial on the left-hand side of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-{x}^{4} & ={x}^{2}(4-{x}^{2}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(2-x)(2+x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we define the function $f(x)$ as\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{2}(2-x)(2+x).\n$$\n\nSo we're now solving the inequality $f(x)<0.$\n\nThe solutions to the equation $f(x)=0$ are $x=-2,$ $x=0$ and $x=2.$ These roots divide the number line into $4$ subintervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,-2),\\,(-2,0),\\,(0,2),\\,(2,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of the intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-2)$ | $(-2,0)$ | $(0,2)$ | $(2,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $2+x$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $2-x$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)<0,$ we look at the bottom row to determine where $f(x)$ is negative.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is negative on the intervals $(-\\infty ,-2)$ and $(2,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $f(x)<0$ for all $x\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (2,\\infty ).$" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318639 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318640 13194139534904 true] [17592186318639 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318641 13194139534904 true] [17592186318639 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318642 13194139534904 true] [17592186318639 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318643 13194139534904 true] [17592186318639 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318644 13194139534904 true] [17592186318639 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534904 true] [17592186318639 1041 "selection" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318639 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318640 13194139534904 true] [17592186318639 1110 #uuid "a067b33e-b3c3-54ef-bb49-636c14cb4dd4" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318640 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (2,\\infty )" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318640 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534904 true] [17592186318640 1111 #uuid "50b9aa5d-1540-5570-a58c-3ea91f88966d" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318641 1034 "x\\in (-2,2)" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318641 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534904 true] [17592186318641 1111 #uuid "0d00dc17-b7a2-5304-b27d-74453684d381" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318642 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,-2)" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318642 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534904 true] [17592186318642 1111 #uuid "a0a0250e-5663-59fd-a9bb-8322e581b403" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318643 1034 "x\\in (-2,0)\\cup (0,2)" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318643 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534904 true] [17592186318643 1111 #uuid "3772762f-807c-5a76-8b08-94d7227dc126" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318644 1034 "x\\in (0,2)\\cup (2,\\infty )" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318644 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534904 true] [17592186318644 1111 #uuid "a02b09dc-c0ce-555c-8de1-44295f60cf3a" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318645 1017 #edb/ref 17592186318646 13194139534904 true] [17592186318645 1017 #edb/ref 17592186318649 13194139534904 true] [17592186318645 1089 "q-281744" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318645 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534904 true] [17592186318645 1100 "Solve the inequality $-2{x}^{3}+16\\ge 0.$\n\n$x\\in $\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$]$" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318645 1113 #uuid "bdc1bcec-90d2-5286-8dfa-ef1e66c75d7f" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318645 1145 "First, we factor the polynomial on the left-hand side of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{3}+16 & =-2({x}^{3}-8) \\\\  & =-2(x-2)({x}^{2}+2x+4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we define the function $f(x)$ as\n\n$$\nf(x)=-2(x-2)({x}^{2}+2x+4).\n$$\n\nSo we're now solving the inequality $f(x)\\ge 0.$ The solution to the equation $f(x)=0$ is $x=2.$  This root divides the number line into $2$ subintervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,2)\\,,\\,(2,\\infty )\n$$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of the intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,2)$ | $(2,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-2$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| $x-2$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| ${x}^{2}+2x+4$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)\\ge 0,$ we look at the bottom row to determine where $f(x)$ is positive.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is positive on the interval $(-\\infty ,2).$ \n\nTherefore, remembering that the root is also a solution, we conclude that $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in (-\\infty ,2].$" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318646 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318647 13194139534904 true] [17592186318646 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318648 13194139534904 true] [17592186318646 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534904 true] [17592186318646 1041 "field-1" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318646 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318648 13194139534904 true] [17592186318646 1110 #uuid "3b953e31-a404-575e-a663-8686105a1509" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318647 1034 "0" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318647 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534904 true] [17592186318647 1111 #uuid "3ef8e42b-dd3d-5f65-8dd8-afeaec69dfc5" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318648 1034 "-\\infty" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318648 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534904 true] [17592186318648 1111 #uuid "960023ce-6c22-5b9b-9783-27c17787f677" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318649 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318650 13194139534904 true] [17592186318649 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534904 true] [17592186318649 1041 "field-2" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318649 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318650 13194139534904 true] [17592186318649 1110 #uuid "637fc4be-db86-51fe-894d-dac22365a833" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318650 1034 "2" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318650 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534904 true] [17592186318650 1111 #uuid "2f88d3fc-fc28-50fb-8e4e-e824df01bbba" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318651 1017 #edb/ref 17592186318652 13194139534904 true] [17592186318651 1017 #edb/ref 17592186318654 13194139534904 true] [17592186318651 1017 #edb/ref 17592186318656 13194139534904 true] [17592186318651 1017 #edb/ref 17592186318658 13194139534904 true] [17592186318651 1017 #edb/ref 17592186318660 13194139534904 true] [17592186318651 1089 "q-282514" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318651 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534904 true] [17592186318651 1100 "Solve the inequality ${x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}>4{x}^{5}+8{x}^{4}.$\n\n$x\\in (-\\infty ,$\n{{field-1}}$)⋃\\,($\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$)⋃\\,($\n{{field-4}}$,$\n{{field-5}}\n$)$" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318651 1113 #uuid "2df07d8c-b2fb-594c-8103-3989dd07f7cf" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318651 1145 "Moving all the terms to the left-hand side and factoring the resulting polynomial, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2} & >4{x}^{5}+8{x}^{4} \\\\ {x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-4{x}^{5}-8{x}^{4} & >0 \\\\ -4{x}^{5}-8{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2} & >0 \\\\ {x}^{2}(-4{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+x+2) & >0 \\\\ {x}^{2}(-4{x}^{2}(x+2)+(x+2)) & >0 \\\\ {x}^{2}(x+2)(-4{x}^{2}+1) & >0 \\\\ {x}^{2}(x+2)(1-4{x}^{2}) & >0 \\\\ {x}^{2}(x+2)(1-2x)(1+2x) & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we define the function $f(x)$ as\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{2}(x+2)(1-2x)(1+2x).\n$$\n\nSo we're now solving the inequality $f(x)>0.$\n\nThe solutions to the equation $f(x)=0$ are $x=-2$, $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$, $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$ These roots divide the number line into $5$ subintervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,-2),\\,(-2,-\\frac{1}{2}),\\,(-\\frac{1}{2},0),\\,(0,\\frac{1}{2}),\\,(\\frac{1}{2},\\infty )\n$$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of the intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-2)$ | $(-2,-\\frac{1}{2})$ | $(-\\frac{1}{2},0)$ | $(0,\\frac{1}{2})$ | $(\\frac{1}{2},\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x+2$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $1-2x$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| $1+2x$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)>0,$ we look at the bottom row to determine where $f(x)$ is positive.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is positive on the intervals $(-\\infty ,-2),$ $(-\\frac{1}{2},0)$ and $(0,\\frac{1}{2}).$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $f(x)>0$ for all $x\\in (-\\infty ,-2)⋃(-\\frac{1}{2},0)⋃(0,\\frac{1}{2}).$" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318652 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318653 13194139534904 true] [17592186318652 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534904 true] [17592186318652 1041 "field-1" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318652 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318653 13194139534904 true] [17592186318652 1110 #uuid "6dcdfcdd-76ab-51ab-bad8-ab44ab0881ae" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318653 1034 "-2" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318653 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534904 true] [17592186318653 1111 #uuid "e225b53e-81af-58bb-8ca7-e82f811439a2" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318654 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318655 13194139534904 true] [17592186318654 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534904 true] [17592186318654 1041 "field-2" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318654 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318655 13194139534904 true] [17592186318654 1110 #uuid "36a4d6cb-a5fb-5ede-8ec8-8e134a471449" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318655 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318655 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534904 true] [17592186318655 1111 #uuid "0be97b26-3083-5466-ba2e-8a4ce54f69e6" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318657 13194139534904 true] [17592186318656 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534904 true] [17592186318656 1041 "field-3" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318656 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318657 13194139534904 true] [17592186318656 1110 #uuid "d909e8be-2f13-5b87-b7c4-f1664b7912ba" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318657 1034 "0" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318657 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534904 true] [17592186318657 1111 #uuid "4e18a944-f7a5-54c4-90ee-dfe2fae70b8c" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318659 13194139534904 true] [17592186318658 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534904 true] [17592186318658 1041 "field-4" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318658 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318659 13194139534904 true] [17592186318658 1110 #uuid "68b4dc1d-d13f-5c36-8271-b48b52683a7e" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318659 1034 "0" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318659 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534904 true] [17592186318659 1111 #uuid "4135142b-80bb-55a2-aad2-d3b8f234d474" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318660 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318661 13194139534904 true] [17592186318660 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534904 true] [17592186318660 1041 "field-5" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318660 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318661 13194139534904 true] [17592186318660 1110 #uuid "5c4d23e2-afdf-5347-9919-87e1f991e0aa" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318661 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318661 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534904 true] [17592186318661 1111 #uuid "c2bc5c3a-2d4c-54b4-b715-106b2d4bfd44" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318662 1017 #edb/ref 17592186318663 13194139534904 true] [17592186318662 1089 "q-40225" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318662 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534904 true] [17592186318662 1100 "Solve the inequality ${x}^{3}-16x<0.$" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318662 1113 #uuid "09e851f1-b681-584d-81f8-586cfcdbdf9b" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318662 1145 "First, we factor the polynomial on the left-hand side of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-16x & =x({x}^{2}-16) \\\\  & =x(x+4)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we define the function $f(x)$ as\n\n$$\nf(x)=x(x+4)(x-4).\n$$\n\nSo we're now solving the inequality $f(x)<0.$\n\nThe solutions to the equation $f(x)=0$ are $x=-4,$ $x=0$ and $x=4.$ These roots divide the number line into $4$ subintervals: \n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,-4),\\,(-4,0),\\,(0,4),\\,(4,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of the intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-4)$ | $(-4,0)$ | $(0,4)$ | $(4,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x+4$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x-4$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)<0,$ we look at the bottom row to determine where $f(x)$ is negative.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is negative on the intervals $(-\\infty ,-4)$ and $(0,4).$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $f(x)<0$ for all $x\\in (-\\infty ,-4)\\cup (0,4).$" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318663 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318664 13194139534904 true] [17592186318663 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318665 13194139534904 true] [17592186318663 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318666 13194139534904 true] [17592186318663 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318667 13194139534904 true] [17592186318663 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318668 13194139534904