 divide the number line into $3$ subintervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,-3),\\,(-3,3),\\,(3,\\infty )\n$$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of the intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-3)$ | $(-3,3)$ | $(3,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}+3$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x+3$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x-3$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)\\ge 0,$ we look at the bottom row to determine where $f(x)$ is positive.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is positive on the intervals $(-\\infty ,-3)$ and $(3,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, remembering that the roots are also solutions, we conclude that $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in (-\\infty ,-3]\\cup [3,\\infty ).$" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318671 13194139534904 true] [17592186318670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318672 13194139534904 true] [17592186318670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318673 13194139534904 true] [17592186318670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318674 13194139534904 true] [17592186318670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318675 13194139534904 true] [17592186318670 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534904 true] [17592186318670 1041 "selection" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318670 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318675 13194139534904 true] [17592186318670 1110 #uuid "e97c3e16-8ca6-54e2-9960-2fdbd706b35c" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318671 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,-9]\\cup [9,\\infty )" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318671 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534904 true] [17592186318671 1111 #uuid "5c0ba8ce-7726-5ef9-8b39-c81ab4dd4433" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318672 1034 "x\\in [-9,9]" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318672 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534904 true] [17592186318672 1111 #uuid "b93ba36b-2ece-5c42-b7ed-47ae391c65f4" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318673 1034 "x\\in [-3,3]" 13194139534904 true] [17592186318673 